// ============================================================================
// 02 - Full request timeline for a narrow window
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose : raw, unaggregated, chronological view of everything that hit the
//           app during a short window. This is how you read the actual story:
//           recon -> probe -> exploit attempt -> follow-up.
// Use it  : after query 01 hands you a suspicious timestamp. Keep the window
//           SHORT (20-30 min) - this returns one row per request.
// Table   : AppServiceHTTPLogs
//
// TUNABLES:
//   datetime(...) .. datetime(...) -> the window. UTC. Format also accepts
//                                     seconds: datetime(2026-09-02 00:05:30)
//   project                        -> add CsHost, Cookie, Referer, Result,
//                                     ScBytes, ComputerName as needed
//   add `| where CIp == "x.x.x.x"` -> focus on one attacker
//   sort asc                       -> keep asc; chronology is the point
// ============================================================================
AppServiceHTTPLogs
| where TimeGenerated between (datetime(2026-09-02 00:05) .. datetime(2026-09-02 00:25))
| project TimeGenerated, CIp, CsMethod, CsUriStem, CsUriQuery, ScStatus, UserAgent, TimeTaken
| sort by TimeGenerated asc
